{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Scope: `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/**` (38 files) and `src/rebar/llm/workflow/**` (26 files). ~230 lines leave of 24,304 LOC — only 0.9%, because this subtree's prose is unusually load-bearing (fail-open/fail-closed contracts, byte-compat pins, patch-seam invariants).\n\n36 of 38 history blocks already cite a ticket id, so most of the work is 'reduce to the citation'. Only two are costly: untracked follow-ups in `production_batch_runner.py` that must be filed first.\n\nVerified stale: SIX sites say 'the deterministic floor (P1-P9)' while `DET_CHECKS` has 11 entries and `registry.CANONICAL_DET` runs P1..P11; `orchestrator.py:9` additionally misstates which checks block. `reuse.py:36-37` cites four line numbers, all four wrong.\n\nThree new ADRs: the unversioned additive-only attestation manifest; the Burr tripwire (a 4-condition adoption trigger list spread across three docstrings, with a test asserting the prose exists); gate context is never elided (including a WITHDRAWN alternative documented as a signed-false-PASS vector).\n\nBiggest headroom win: `workflow/executor.py` 791 -> ~769, almost entirely from three 'so this module stays under the module-size cap' notes.\n\nByte-pinned json.dumps rationale in attest.py/pass1.py is maintainer-blessed and must stay verbatim — converging it would invalidate live attestations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured-fact and anti-refactor warnings stay verbatim\n## CORRECTION (plan-review preempt + test-safety, parent 373f disposition vocabulary)\n\nThis is the most load-bearing shard (fail-open/fail-closed contracts, byte-compat pins, a\ndocstring pinned by a live test). Superseding ACs below encode the 373f disposition rules plus\nthe specific test-safety and byte-pin constraints this subtree requires.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] Every substantial in-scope comment unit is dispositioned into exactly one parent-373f\n      label: RELOCATE (to an ADR / docs / ticket, reduced to a one-line citation), DELETE, KEEP,\n      DO_NOT_MOVE, or CORRECT-IN-PLACE.\n- [ ] Decision rule CORRECT-vs-DELETE: a comment documenting CURRENT runtime behavior / a live\n      invariant is CORRECTED in place; DELETE only when its referent no longer exists. Every\n      DELETE records its reason (referenced-artifact-gone / superseded) in the commit body or a\n      ticket comment.\n- [ ] The stale \"P1–P9\" enumerations are CORRECTED to \"P1–P11\" ONLY where the site claims to\n      enumerate the CURRENT full DET floor (CANONICAL_DET is P1..P11; DET_CHECKS has 11 entries,\n      P10/P11 in det_clarity). Where \"P1–P9\" deliberately names the pre-clarity STATIC floor as a\n      seam boundary (e.g. a \"runs BEFORE / not a DET_CHECKS entry\" note), it is KEPT — read each\n      site's context, do not blind-replace. `orchestrator.py:9`'s misstatement of WHICH checks\n      block is corrected to the real blocking set (P1 / P5-cycle / P8 / P10 / P11, per\n      det_floor.py:733).\n- [ ] `reuse.py:36-37`'s four wrong line-number citations are corrected to the actual lines (or\n      the citation is generalized to the symbol name if the target moves).\n- [ ] TEST-SAFETY (Burr tripwire): `tests/unit/workflow/test_executor_tripwire.py` asserts, on\n      the executor source, that `\"burr\"` appears AND at least four of `1.`/`2.`/`3.`/`4.` survive,\n      and that the fan-out module's text contains `\"rationale\"`. The tripwire prose may be\n      compressed/reworded and its full rationale RELOCATED to a new ADR, but executor.py MUST\n      still contain `\"burr\"` + the four-item numbered trigger list, and the fan-out module MUST\n      still contain `\"rationale\"`. Do NOT edit this test. Run it and confirm green after the edit.\n- [ ] BYTE-PIN (DO_NOT_MOVE, verbatim): the byte-identical `json.dumps` rationale in\n      `attest.py` and `pass1.py` (bug 96d1 / story 9374 — a signed hash must byte-exactly match\n      the legacy recomputation; converging or rewording it would invalidate live attestations)\n      stays verbatim. Do not touch it.\n- [ ] Untracked follow-ups: any prose in `workflow/production_batch_runner.py` describing future\n      work WITHOUT a ticket id is FILED as a rebar ticket and linked `discovered_from` this\n      ticket BEFORE its comment is collapsed to the new id. (Report the ids you file.)\n- [ ] Three new ADRs are created with unique unused numbers (>= 0064): the additive-only\n      unversioned attestation manifest; the Burr adoption tripwire (fuller home for the executor\n      trigger list); and the \"gate context is never elided\" contract (INCLUDING the WITHDRAWN\n      alternative documented as a signed-false-PASS vector — keep that warning). Each ADR EXISTS\n      and is committed before any comment citing it is collapsed. Provenance line: epic b5bc;\n      ticket ad16.\n- [ ] `workflow/executor.py` may shrink (the three self-referential \"so this module stays under\n      the module-size cap\" notes are removable narration) but MUST stay <= 800 lines and MUST NOT\n      exceed the cap.\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands;\n      lint/type pragmas and test-introspected docstrings are DO_NOT_MOVE.\n- [ ] The actual recovered comment-line count is measured (by diff) and recorded on this ticket\n      as an OUTPUT, not a target.\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the full test suite AND `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass unchanged."}},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786183443326933001,"uuid":"826adca5-6cdb-44b9-b62a-fabe29ba6c94"}